#![allow(clippy::excessive_precision)]
//! Golden-parity test for the reference's **NPR block** (`GUI_GAP_REGISTER.md`
//! RN-01): the ten "Painter" hand-drawn styles (reference HTML lines
//! 7907-7958), the multi-sun light rig (8357-8363) and the coastal
//! wave lines' distance transform (7398-7414).
//!
//! Extracted by slicing those three ranges out of the frozen reference and
//! running them under Node's `vm`, the same technique `golden_parity_render.rs`
//! and every other golden test in this crate use. The extractor asserts each
//! slice's first and last line against expected text before running it --
//! this repo's own working rules record four subsystems bitten by a silently
//! wrong or silently empty slice.
//!
//! **The fixtures are shaped, not sampled.** Sixteen cells reach the branches
//! the styles actually hide in: contours on and off an index line, hachure
//! either side of 0.12, crosshatch across all three darkness bands *and*
//! sitting just inside each of the three gates that separate them, ink both
//! either side of its 0.18 edge gate and 0.005 above it, and a fully-black
//! and a fully-white cell for the clamps. Each style is additionally run
//! **alone** before the stacked cases, so a broken style cannot hide inside a
//! stack, and the contour interval gets four settings of its own — the legacy
//! fraction, a real metre interval, the `peakM || 4000` fallback, and both
//! ends of the `min(0.2, max(0.001, ...))` clamp.
//!
//! The last four cases and the last three settings are the **mutation
//! sweep's** doing: `dark > 0.42` -> `0.43`, `edge > 0.18` -> `0.19`, the
//! `4000` fallback and both clamp ends all survived against the original
//! twelve cases, which crossed those branches without ever landing inside one
//! of their narrow windows. The three greys are neutral, so `dark` is exactly
//! `1 - channel/255` rather than approximately it.

